diff --git a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/configuration.mdx b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/configuration.mdx
index 1975a43af93641af4d58849ea730183812a5ea23..54184b0fa281062dcef2bf119de6b24e45a3fecc 100644
--- a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/configuration.mdx
+++ b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/configuration.mdx
@@ -550,14 +550,16 @@ Restricting `cjk_ime_agents` avoids showing an extra hardware cursor in unrelate
 
 ## Prefix input source switching
 
-On macOS and Windows, Herdr can temporarily switch to an ASCII-capable input source while prefix commands and prefix-launched modes are active:
+On macOS, Windows, and Linux with niri/Wayland and Fcitx5, Herdr can temporarily switch to an ASCII-capable input source while prefix commands and prefix-launched modes are active:
 
 ```toml
 [experimental]
 switch_ascii_input_source_in_prefix = true
 ```
 
-On macOS this switches to the current ASCII-capable keyboard layout; on Windows it switches the IME to English (ASCII) input. Herdr restores the previous input source when returning to terminal input or entering a text field. This setting has no effect on other platforms.
+On macOS this switches to the current ASCII-capable keyboard layout; on Windows it switches the IME to English (ASCII) input. On niri/Wayland it deactivates Fcitx5 while prefix mode is active, including the default `Ctrl+B` prefix. Configure an English keyboard layout as the first input method in your Fcitx5 group. The foreground client needs access to the session D-Bus and a valid `NIRI_SOCKET`; no `fcitx5-remote` command is required.
+
+Herdr restores the previous input source when returning to terminal input or entering a text field. On niri, restoration requires the same window to be focused and Fcitx5 to remain inactive. Switching is asynchronous and best effort; unavailable desktop services leave the input source unchanged. This setting has no effect on other platforms.
 
 :::caution[Windows support is Korean IME only]
 On Windows, support is currently limited to the Korean IME. With an IME for any other language, this setting leaves the input source unchanged.
diff --git a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/ja/configuration.mdx b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/ja/configuration.mdx
